---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { href } from "../lib/paths";
---
<Layout title="ADHD, asthma, and college-student care in Blacksburg | Kin & Campus" description="Personalized pediatric care in Blacksburg for Virginia Tech students: ADHD and other medication follow-up, asthma, allergies, acne, sexual health, sick visits, and university forms.">
<div class="w ph"><div class="eyebrow">Our care</div><h1>ADHD, asthma, and college-student care in Blacksburg.</h1><p class="lead">A board-certified pediatrician who treats the conditions they already have and the ones that show up on campus. We are not a 24/7 line, not a counseling center, and not the emergency room.</p></div>
<div class="w"><img class="photo" src={href("photos/campus-aerial.jpg")} width="800" height="450" alt="Campus and the surrounding hills, seen from above">
<div class="grid">
<div class="card" id="adhd"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-leaf"/></svg><h3>ADHD</h3><p>Ongoing prescriptions and follow-up for students who already have a diagnosis. Campus clinics often refer ADHD medication to a community doctor. We can be that doctor in town.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="mental-health"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg><h3>Mental-health medication follow-up</h3><p>Anxiety and depression medications that started at home. We manage the prescription and refer when they need therapy. We are not a counseling center.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="acne"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-moon"/></svg><h3>Acne</h3><p>Common, treatable, and easy to let slide when they are busy. Simple plans they can keep during the semester.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="allergies"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-compass"/></svg><h3>Allergies</h3><p>Environmental and food allergies. Refills, action plans, and what to do when Blacksburg pollen or a dining hall surprise hits.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="asthma"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg><h3>Asthma</h3><p>Controllers, rescue inhalers, and a plan that does not lapse over winter break. The hometown doctor stays copied.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="forms"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg><h3>University, housing, and athletics forms</h3><p>Immunization paperwork, SSD housing letters, club and sports physicals, and travel health forms. The paperwork that otherwise sits in a parent group text.</p></div>
<div class="card" id="sexual-health"><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><h3>Sexual and reproductive health</h3><p>Confidential contraception, STI testing, and questions they may not want to put on a parent insurance portal. Their chart, their choice about who we tell.</p></div>
</div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 360 360" role="img" aria-label="Portrait placeholder"><rect width="360" height="360" rx="28" fill="#EADFCB"/><circle cx="180" cy="140" r="56" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M70 330q110-150 220 0z" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="270" cy="86" r="20" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="8"/></svg>
<div><div class="eyebrow">The physician</div><h2>A board-certified pediatrician in Blacksburg.</h2><p class="lead">Personalized medical care for Virginia Tech students, coordinated with the hometown physician. Direct text. Visits eight minutes from campus. The year-long plan held here.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">A year in town</div><h2>Care from August through May.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="num">August</div><p>Initial parent intake conversation, followed by an in-person baseline visit with the student to establish care before classes start.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">The Semester</div><p>Sick visits, prescription refills, and check-ins around holiday transitions.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">Finals</div><p>A look at sleep, stress, and whether medications are still being taken during testing weeks.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">May</div><p>A year-end clinical summary to the hometown physician so August starts from a full page.</p></div></div>
<p style="margin-top:36px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
